To decouple the size of the reservation table from the AXI ID width and eliminate the constraint of having a unique and consistent ID for each master, we add a parameter that uses the AXI user signal as the reservation ID instead of the AXI ID signal. This enables us to add ID width converters in front of the ATUN and that we do not have to allocate space in the reservation table for masters which do not issue atomics.

To enable this feature, set `AXI_USER_AS_ID` to one and specify which bits in the AW channel's user signal will be used for the reservation ID with: `reservation id = aw_user[AXI_USER_ID_MSB:AXI_USER_ID_LSB]`

